                <pb facs="0463" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296A/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sackett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-19T19:00:00+01:00">November 19, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 19—2:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>223. [Paraphrase.] With reference to the Embassy’s No. 221, 19th of November, 2
                    p.m. The agreement with France has been reached. I have been officially notified
                    of this since filing the reference telegram. Today, the Germans mailed the note
                    to Basel. [End paraphrase.] It will be published Saturday. A copy will be given
                    me tomorrow at noon. Shall I send full translation?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
